DS3D gst is the GStreamer glue layer for DS3D. It carries a `ds3d::datamap`
inside a GstBuffer as DS3D meta, and it wraps custom `ds3d::` modules into
ready-to-use GStreamer elements so that a DS3D pipeline can be assembled with
plain GStreamer API or a YAML graph.

`libnvdsgst_3d_gst.so` is built from these source files. Unlike the other DS3D
modules it is not loaded through `custom_lib_path` — it is linked directly by
the DS3D GStreamer plugins and sample apps:

    gst-nvds3dbridge, gst-nvds3dfilter, gst-nvds3dmixer, gst-nvmsgconv
    deepstream-3d-depth-camera, deepstream-3d-lidar-sensor-fusion,
    deepstream-lidar-inference-app, deepstream-can-orientation-app

The main entry points, declared in `includes/ds3d/gst`, are:

    NvDs3D_CreateDataLoaderSrc(config, ...)     wrap a ds3d::dataloader in appsrc
    NvDs3D_CreateDataRenderSink(config, ...)    wrap a ds3d::datarender in appsink
    NvDs3D_GstAppSrcSetDataloader               bind a dataloader to an existing appsrc
    NvDs3D_GstAppSinkSetDataRender              bind a datarender to an existing appsink
    NvDs3D_CreateGstBuf / NvDs3D_UpdateDataMap  put or update a datamap in a GstBuffer
    NvDs3D_IsDs3DBuf / NvDs3D_Find1stDataMap    DS3D meta access on a GstBuffer
    NvDs3D_BatchMeta_SetDataMapAsMeta           attach a datamap to NvDsBatchMeta

The element-configuration YAML that these helpers consume is the same
`type:`/`custom_lib_path:`/`custom_create_function:`/`config_body:` form used by
the other DS3D modules.

More details, refer to the DeepStream SDK documentation for section of "DeepStream 3D Custom Manual".
https://docs.nvidia.com/metropolis/deepstream/dev-guide/text/DS_3D_Custom_Manual.html

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pre-requisites:
- libnvds_3d_common.so (build and install ds3d/common first)
- libgstreamer1.0 and libgstreamer-plugins-base1.0 Development packages
- libyaml-cpp Development package
- CUDA Runtime

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Compiling and installing this lib:
- Export CUDA_VER, then build. sudo -E keeps the variable for make.
  $ export CUDA_VER=13.2 # x86, Jetson and SBSA. For IGX Thor, CUDA_VER=13.0
  $ make && sudo -E make install
- Verify `libnvdsgst_3d_gst.so` exist and installed well.

NOTE: Compiling does not need root. Install with `sudo -E` so CUDA_VER is kept. Skip sudo when already root (for example inside a container).
